# Domain Crawler — the crawler-monitor unit's access to NVMe (T-089, spec §10.3).
#
# The wear alert of monitor (internal/monitor/alerts.go, T-080) reads the
# health log with the NVME_IOCTL_ADMIN_CMD ioctl; the ioctl requires opening
# the controller char node (/dev/nvme0) for writing. The kernel default is
# root:root 0600: the rule hands the controller nodes to the dedicated
# nvme-smart group, which the drop-in crawler-monitor.service.d/90-nvme-smart.conf
# adds to the unit (SupplementaryGroups).
#
# A separate group instead of the existing disk one: access exactly to the
# NVMe nodes, without rights to other block devices. Write access to the node
# is the kernel's requirement for admin commands; in fact only log reads happen.
#
# Installation (docs/disks.md, deploy/smartd/README.md):
#   install -m 0644 99-crawler-nvme.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   udevadm control --reload && udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=nvme
SUBSYSTEM=="nvme", KERNEL=="nvme[0-9]*", GROUP="nvme-smart", MODE="0660"
